LIP-SYNC MUSIC PERFORMANCE SHOT.

@image1 is the character sheet. Use it as the sole source of identity: same face, same facial structure, same hairstyle, same proportions from every angle it shows. Do not restyle, do not change age or ethnicity, do not swap the hair. Exactly one instance of this character on screen, no duplicates in the background.

@image2 is the key visual. Take the location, set dressing, time of day, lighting direction, lighting intensity and colour grading from it, and hold them steady for the whole shot. It is a look reference only: do not copy any person out of it, and never let it override the identity in @image1.

@audio1 is the vocal to perform. The character sings exactly this audio. Match mouth shape, jaw opening and tongue position to its phonemes frame by frame: full lip closure on m / b / p, teeth-to-lip contact on f / v, open vowels on sustained notes, and a still, relaxed mouth during instrumental gaps and breaths. Never mouth words that are not in @audio1.

PERFORMANCE: breathing, head bobs, shoulder motion, eyebrow lifts and micro-expressions follow the rhythm, dynamics and emotion of the vocal. Natural blinks, consistent teeth and inner mouth, eyes alive and engaged. Body motion is present but never louder than the singing.

QUALITY: photoreal continuity, stable identity, no face morphing, no identity drift, no warped or extra fingers, no duplicated subject, no on-screen text, no lyric captions, no subtitles, no watermark, no split screen.
